# Millonarios Fan App PRD
## Template-Based Sports App (iOS)

---

## 1. Product Overview

The Millonarios Fan App is a content-first mobile application that aggregates all relevant information about a football club into a single platform.

It combines:
- News and media aggregation
- Live match data and standings
- Community discussion (forum + karma)
- Future ticket marketplace

The system is designed as a reusable template that can be easily adapted to any football team.

---

## 2. Product Goals

### Primary Goal
Create the best single place to follow a football team.

### Secondary Goals
- Build a daily habit loop through feed and notifications
- Enable community trust via karma system
- Prepare infrastructure for marketplace monetization

---

## 3. User Personas

### Casual Fan
- Wants quick updates
- Checks scores and headlines

### Engaged Fan
- Consumes content regularly
- Participates in discussions

### Super Fan (Future Seller)
- Active contributor
- Builds karma over time
- Interested in buying/selling tickets

---

## 4. Core Features

### 4.1 Aggregated Feed (Core Feature)

#### Description
A chronological feed aggregating:
- YouTube videos (selected channels)
- News articles (manual sources via RSS)
- Social media posts (public APIs)
- Optional match events

#### Behavior
- Strict chronological order (latest first)
- No ranking algorithm in v1

#### Filters
- All
- News
- Videos
- Social
- Matches

#### Search
- Keyword-based search across feed items

#### Data Model

FeedItem {
  id
  team_id
  type (news | video | social | match_event)
  title
  description
  source_name
  source_url
  thumbnail
  published_at
  metadata (json)
}

---

### 4.2 Matches, Fixtures, Standings

#### Features
- Upcoming matches
- Live scores
- Match stats
- League standings

#### Data Source
- SofaScore API (paid)

#### Screens
- Fixtures list
- Match detail (live)
- Standings table

---

### 4.3 Community Forum + Karma

#### Features
- Create posts
- Comment threads
- Upvote system

#### Karma System
- +1 karma per upvote received

#### Future Enhancements
- Anti-spam weighting
- Reputation tiers

---

### 4.4 Marketplace (Phase 2)

#### Unlock Requirements
- Account age ≥ 1 year
- Karma ≥ defined threshold

#### v1
- Listing posts only (no transactions)

#### Future
- Escrow payments
- Identity verification
- Platform fee

---

### 4.5 Notifications

#### Configurable Alerts
- Match start
- Goals (live)
- Breaking news
- Forum replies
- Marketplace activity

---

## 5. System Architecture

### 5.1 Multi-App Strategy

Each team will have a separate app instance.

Shared components:
- Backend
- Codebase
- Infrastructure

---

### 5.2 Team Configuration Layer

TeamConfig {
  team_id
  name
  colors
  logo
  leagues
  youtube_channels[]
  news_sources[]
  social_accounts[]
}

This enables fast replication for new teams.

---

### 5.3 Feed Ingestion System

#### Pipeline
1. Fetch sources
2. Normalize content
3. Deduplicate
4. Store as FeedItems

#### Sources
- YouTube API
- RSS feeds (news)
- Social media APIs

#### Frequency
- Every 5–10 minutes

---

## 6. Tech Stack Recommendation

### Frontend
- React Native (Expo)

### Backend
- Supabase (database, auth, storage)

### APIs
- SofaScore (matches)
- YouTube API
- Social APIs (X, Instagram if available)
- RSS feeds

---

## 7. Design Direction

- Dark mode first
- Strong team identity (colors, branding)
- Card-based feed layout
- Large typography
- Smooth animations
- Minimal reliance on generic UI patterns

Goal: feel like an official club product, not a generic sports app.

---

## 8. Monetization

### Phase 1
- Subscription:
  - No ads
  - Premium features
  - Enhanced notifications

### Phase 2
- Marketplace transaction fee (5%–15%)

---

## 9. MVP Scope

### Must Have
- Feed aggregation
- Matches and standings
- Basic forum

### Not in MVP
- Marketplace transactions
- Advanced moderation
- Complex ranking algorithms

---

## 10. Risks

- Feed aggregation complexity
- Social API limitations
- Marketplace trust and fraud prevention (future)

---

## 11. Roadmap

### Phase 1 (4–6 weeks)
- Feed system
- Matches integration
- Core UI

### Phase 2
- Forum + karma system

### Phase 3
- Marketplace features

---

## 12. Key Insight

The core value of the product is not the UI.

It is:
- The aggregation engine
- The community layer

If those are strong, the product becomes defensible and scalable.

